<title>USA: TVA shuts Watts Bar power plant for repair.</title>
<headline>TVA shuts Watts Bar power plant for repair.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>TVA Nuclear has again shut its 1,170 megawatt (MW) Watts Bar nuclear power plant for repairs, Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The plant, in Spring City, Tenn., was shut Monday after a leak was discovered in a &quot;main condenser tube,&quot; NRC said in its daily status report.</p>
<p>The unit had just come back to full power Monday after suddenly tripping off line Friday when the main feedwater pumps automatically shut down.</p>
<p>The company as a matter of policy declines to comment on its power plant operations.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk + 212 859 1628))</p>
